  {
   "title": "III. Kung or kapág",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "p",
     "t": "To show an action that is **happening in the present** or **will still happen in the future**, *when* is translated with **kung** or **kapág**. The shortened form of kapág is **pag**."
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "t": "In this sense the English word **if** has a similar meaning, so one Tagalog sentence can be translated both ways."
    },
    {
     "type": "examples",
     "items": [
      {
       "tl": "Kung áalis ka, sásáma ako sa iyó.",
       "en": "When you leave, I shall go with you. / If you leave, I shall go with you.",
       "parts": [
        [
         "Kung",
         "when / if",
         "other"
        ],
        [
         "áalis",
         "will leave",
         "pred"
        ],
        [
         "ka",
         "you",
         "pron"
        ],
        [
         "sásáma",
         "shall go with",
         "pred"
        ],
        [
         "ako",
         "I",
         "pron"
        ],
        [
         "sa",
         "(with)",
         "marker"
        ],
        [
         "iyó",
         "you",
         "pron"
        ]
       ]
      },
      {
       "tl": "Naghihilík siya kapág natutulog.",
       "en": "He snores when he is sleeping.",
       "parts": [
        [
         "Naghihilík",
         "snores",
         "pred"
        ],
        [
         "siya",
         "he",
         "pron"
        ],
        [
         "kapág",
         "when",
         "other"
        ],
        [
         "natutulog",
         "is sleeping",
         "pred"
        ]
       ]
      },
      {
       "tl": "Magtatampó ako pag aalís ka.",
       "en": "I will be displeased if you leave.",
       "parts": [
        [
         "Magtatampó",
         "will be displeased",
         "pred"
        ],
        [
         "ako",
         "I",
         "pron"
        ],
        [
         "pag",
         "if (short for kapág)",
         "other"
        ],
        [
         "aalís",
         "will leave",
         "pred"
        ],
        [
         "ka",
         "you",
         "pron"
        ]
       ]
      }
     ],
     "title": "Kung / kapág / pag"
    },
    {
     "type": "box",
     "kind": "tip",
     "title": "Spelling",
     "t": "The book writes **áalis** in the first sentence and **aalís** in the third. Both mean *will leave*."
    },
